1
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:07,001
A fix somebody made on this machine is still here — and something has moved since.

2
00:00:07,011 --> 00:00:11,011
PODSHL says so at the start. It undoes nothing by itself.

3
00:00:12,074 --> 00:00:13,074
Ask about something that is broken.

4
00:00:13,245 --> 00:00:15,245


5
00:00:16,338 --> 00:00:18,338
The project, by name.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:24,800
engram publishes support files in its own repository. Nothing was installed for this.

7
00:00:25,262 --> 00:00:31,262
It offers to check where this machine got engram from. You can decline.

8
00:00:31,272 --> 00:00:37,272
These are the problems engram says it can answer — their words, not a guess.

9
00:00:38,334 --> 00:00:41,334
Search stopped finding things it used to find.

10
00:00:41,796 --> 00:00:49,796


11
00:00:49,805 --> 00:00:56,805
Now it asks. Item by item, with the reason, and what it would read.

12
00:00:56,815 --> 00:00:59,815
Nothing has been sent yet.

13
00:01:00,277 --> 00:01:08,277


14
00:01:08,286 --> 00:01:14,286
Three things only a person can answer. They can be left blank.

15
00:01:16,803 --> 00:01:19,803
Yes — and the reindex was never run.

16
00:01:20,265 --> 00:01:28,265


17
00:01:28,274 --> 00:01:35,274
This is everything that would leave the machine, before it leaves.

18
00:01:35,283 --> 00:01:40,283
Unanswered questions go as unanswered, rather than being left out.

19
00:01:40,745 --> 00:01:50,745


20
00:01:50,755 --> 00:01:56,755
engram's own answer, from the files engram publishes.

21
00:01:56,764 --> 00:02:01,764
The amber line marks what you said, not what was measured.

22
00:02:02,226 --> 00:02:08,226


23
00:02:08,235 --> 00:02:13,235
Whether it worked is the one thing only you can tell them.

24
00:02:13,697 --> 00:02:21,697


25
00:02:21,707 --> 00:02:29,707
And what nothing covers becomes Markdown you take to the project — anonymised, and shown first.

